module-help "
Qt is a cross-platform software development framework for creating
graphical user interfaces, desktop applications, and embedded systems.

Qt provides a comprehensive collection of C++ libraries and development
tools for building modern, portable applications.

This installation includes the open-source Qt 6 framework and its
available submodules, including:

  - Qt Core, GUI, Widgets, Network and Concurrent
  - Qt Quick, QML and Declarative
  - Qt OpenGL and 3D
  - Qt Data Visualization, Charts and Graphs
  - Qt Multimedia, SVG and Image Formats
  - Qt WebEngine and WebChannel
  - Qt SQL, XML and other development components

Qt includes development tools such as moc, rcc, uic, qmake and
Qt CMake integration.

The framework is compiled using GCC 12.3.0 and is intended for
applications requiring a modern C++ development environment,
including scientific visualization and accelerator simulation tools.

Qt is available under open-source licenses, primarily LGPLv3 and
GPLv3, depending on the specific module. Additional third-party
licenses may apply.

Not all Qt components are necessarily available if optional build
dependencies were not satisfied.

Documentation:
  https://doc.qt.io/qt-6.8/

Licensing:
  https://doc.qt.io/qt-6.8/licensing.html
"
